 "rules": {
  "needsTrack": true,
  "needsOneCar": true,
  "notes": "No official page was found that states the entry rule for daily races; treat both flags as probable, not confirmed. Track: a 2024 Traxion guide says you need to own DLC tracks to race them online, and a Dec 2024 Steam forum thread had a player unable to join a beginner daily until they had the new content. Car: at least one car of an eligible class must logically be owned; a forum reply says adding the free McLaren car let a player join beginner races and base-game LMP2 and GTE cars worked for beginners, so owning the track plus any free eligible car should be enough. Free cars (no purchase) include Oreca 07, the GTE cars, Mercedes LMGT3, Mustang LMGT3, McLaren LMGT3 Evo, most Hypercars and the Adess AD25 LMP3 (since v1.3.3, June 2026), which is why LMP3 Fixed is a beginner race. RaceControl Pro+ unlocks all LMU DLC while the subscription is active. Beginner, Intermediate and Advanced are RaceControl safety-rank gates, not ownership gates: Beginner is open to all, Intermediate needs Silver safety rank, Advanced needs Gold. Everyone starts at Bronze for both safety and driver rank. For multi-class series it is not known whether a player needs a car in every class or just one eligible class; assume one. The US Track Pass is meant to include a third US pack (due December 2026, not yet released), and the 2024 Season Pass is no longer sold on Steam."
 },
